{"type":"message","id":"256dfeda","parentId":"60cfc02a","timestamp":"2026-05-26T12:03:39.025Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"exec_ts_ZTI0ODMwYTctNWNkNi00MmZlLTk5OGItZWU1MzllNzJiOWMz","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"total 8\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 bhard bhard 4096 May 26 12:02 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 6 bhard bhard 4096 May 26 12:02 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 bhard bhard    0 May 26 12:02 raw.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 bhard bhard    0 May 26 12:02 validated.json"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":26,"aggregated":"total 8\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 bhard bhard 4096 May 26 12:02 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 6 bhard bhard 4096 May 26 12:02 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 bhard bhard    0 May 26 12:02 raw.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 bhard bhard    0 May 26 12:02 validated.json","cwd":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779797019025}}
{"type":"message","id":"33f6e167","parentId":"256dfeda","timestamp":"2026-05-26T12:03:46.383Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"write_ts_ZTI0ODMwYTctNWNkNi00MmZlLTk5OGItZWU1MzllNzJiOWMz","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"story_id\": \"ondo-finance-founder-nathan-allman-dies-32\",\n  \"topic_theme\": \"Ondo Finance Founder Nathan Allman Passes Away Unexpectedly at 32\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"Ondo Finance Nathan Allman\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"Ondo Finance Founder Nathan Allman Dies Unexpectedly at Age 32\",\n  \"primary_asset\": \"Ondo Finance\",\n  \"chart_coin\": \"ondo-finance\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"CoinTelegraph\",\n    \"CoinDesk\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"https://cointelegraph.com/news/ondo-finance-founder-nathan-allman-passes-away-aged-32\",\n    \"https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/26/ondo-finance-founder-nathan-allman-passes-away\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n    \"Nathan Allman, founder and CEO of pioneering real-world asset (RWA) tokenization firm Ondo Finance, has passed away unexpectedly at the age of 32.\",\n    \"Ondo Finance announced his passing on Monday, May 25, 2026, via a post on X, without disclosing the cause of death. His family has requested privacy.\",\n    \"Ian De Bode, Ondo's longtime president who has managed strategy, product, and day-to-day operations for over two years, will immediately step in as CEO.\",\n    \"Allman founded Ondo Finance in 2021 after working on Goldman Sachs' digital assets team and founding algorithmic crypto hedge fund ChainStreet Capital.\",\n    \"Under Allman's leadership, Ondo grew to manage over $3.5 billion in total value locked (TVL) across tokenized products like USDY (yield-bearing stablecoin) and OUSG (tokenized U.S. Treasury fund).\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"=== SOURCE 1: COINTELEGRAPH ===\\nNathan Allman, the founder and CEO of Ondo Finance and one of the pioneers of blockchain tokenization, has died aged 32.\\n'It is with profound sadness that we announce the unexpected passing of Nathan Allman, Ondo's founder,' Ondo Finance said in an X post on Monday. 'Our hearts are with his family and loved ones.'\\n'Nate's brilliance, humility, and drive shaped every part of what Ondo is today,' Ondo said. 'His belief in the power of technology to create a more open, accessible financial system lives on in everything we build. The impact he had on this industry, and on all of us personally, cannot be overstated.'\\nAllman was key in helping Ondo bring $3.86 billion worth of tokenized real-world assets on-chain in the form of US Treasuries, stocks and commodities. More than 111,680 token holders own a tokenized RWA issued by Ondo.\\nNathan Allman speaking at the Ninth Annual Fintech Conference in Philadelphia in November.\\nThe tokenization movement that Allman contributed to by founding Ondo in 2021 helped capture the attention of Wall Street giants such as BlackRock, who see potential in the technology to make trading and settlement more efficient.\\nAllman previously worked in Goldman Sachs' digital asset team prior to founding Ondo. Before that, he founded the crypto hedge fund ChainStreet Capital, which focused on algorithmic, event-driven trading.\\nOndo said that the company's president, Ian De Bode, would serve as CEO.\\n'It's been an incredibly sad day for Ondo Finance,' De Bode told Cointelegraph. 'Nate was not only an incredible founder and visionary, but also a very close personal friend. He will be missed dearly.'\\n'The mission of Ondo, Nate's mission, has not changed,' he added. 'If Nate were here, he would want to continue executing with excellence. We will make him proud.'\\nOndo vice president and head of marketing, Ben Grossman, said Allman 'was a once-in-a-generation founder and visionary. He was absolutely brilliant, with a vision and drive that shaped the industry and everyone around him. He will be enormously missed.'\\nOndo did not share further details on Allman's death. An Ondo spokesperson said that Allman's family has requested privacy at this time.\\n\\n=== SOURCE 2: COINDESK ===\\nOndo Finance founder Nathan Allman has died unexpectedly, with longtime president Ian De Bode stepping in as CEO.\\nOndo Finance said its founder, Nathan Allman, has died unexpectedly, without disclosing the cause of death.\\nIan De Bode, the firm's longtime president who has overseen strategy, product and daily operations, will become chief executive with the backing of the leadership team.\\nAllman, a Brown graduate and former member of Goldman Sachs's digital assets team, founded Ondo in 2021 and led its growth into a tokenized real-world asset pioneer with $3.5 billion in total value locked and products including the USDY stablecoin and OUSG Treasury fund.\\nOndo Finance founder Nathan Allman has died, the company said in a post on X on Tuesday, without disclosing the cause.\\n'It is with profound sadness that we announce the unexpected passing of Nathan Allman, Ondo's founder. Our hearts are with his family and loved ones,' the company said. 'Nate's brilliance, humility, and drive shaped every part of what Ondo is today. His belief in the power of technology to create a more open, accessible financial system lives on in everything we build.'\\nIan De Bode, Ondo's longtime president who has led strategy, product, and day-to-day operations for over two years, will serve as CEO. De Bode has the full confidence of the leadership team, the company said.\\nAllman, a Brown University graduate, founded Ondo in 2021 after working on Goldman Sachs' digital assets team. Under his leadership, Ondo became a pioneer in tokenized real-world assets, growing total value locked to $3.5 billion.\\nMajor products launched during his tenure include USDY, a yield-bearing stablecoin, OUSG, a tokenized U.S. Treasury fund, and tokenized equities through Ondo Global Markets.\\nThe company said it would continue building what Allman started as the most meaningful way to honor him.\"\n}","path":"/tmp/crypto-run-20260526-120208/research/raw.json"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gemini-3.5-flash","usage":{"input":5745,"output":1451,"cacheRead":19564,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":26760,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779797019029,"responseId":"HIwVaufNDNKQ694P9NLQ8QE"}}
